  {
    "title": "Kauffman Announces Preservation Grant for Capitol Theatre",
    "url": "http://www.repkauffman.com/News/38102/Press-Releases/Kauffman-Announces-Preservation-Grant-for-Capitol-Theatre",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Kauffman Announces Preservation Grant for Capitol Theatre\nJune 11, 2026\nHARRISBURG\n– State Rep. Rob Kauffman (R-Franklin) today announced a $30,000 grant has been awarded to the Capitol Theatre Center Foundation in Chambersburg under the Pennsylvania Historical and Museum Commission’s Keystone Historic Preservation Grant program.\n“The Capitol Theatre Center Foundation continuously works to preserve the historic building, constructed in 1927. It is now a National Historic Landmark, and is a gem in our community, offering cultural events, movies and other entertainment,” said Kauffman.\nThe funding will be used to replace water and sewer lines running beneath the theatre building. The project will ensure historic restoration of underground infrastructure from the building to the street.\nKeystone Historic Preservation Grants provide funding to support projects that identify, preserve, promote, and protect historic and archaeological resources in Pennsylvania for both the benefit of the public and the revitalization of communities. The Capitol Theatre was one of only 38 projects across the state to receive funding under the program, which requires matching funding from the recipient.\nRepresentative Rob Kauffman\n89th District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Tricia Lehman\n717.772.9840\ntlehman@pahousegop.com\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "A state grant of $30,000 was awarded to the Capitol Theatre Center Foundation in Chambersburg through a Pennsylvania Historical and Museum Commission program. The money will fund replacement of water and sewer lines under the 1927 historic building. Rep. Kauffman announced the grant but did not author or sponsor it; the funding came through an existing statewide preservation grant program.",
      "action_type": "statement",
      "topics": [
        "infrastructure",
        "other"
      ],
      "spin_flag": true
    }
  },
  {
    "title": "Franklin County Farmers Invited to Ag Breakfast Hosted by Reichard, Kauffman and Irvin",
    "url": "http://www.repkauffman.com/News/37704/Press-Releases/Franklin-County-Farmers-Invited-to-Ag-Breakfast-Hosted-by-Reichard--Kauffman-and-Irvin",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Franklin County Farmers Invited to Ag Breakfast Hosted by Reichard, Kauffman and Irvin\nMarch 18, 2026\nWAYNESBORO – Reps. Chad Reichard (R-Franklin), Rob Kauffman (R-Franklin) and Rich Irvin (R-Franklin/Huntingdon) will host an Ag Breakfast next month to bring together farmers, agricultural professionals, agribusiness leaders and residents, including those working across the broader agriculture and food systems, to discuss issues impacting Pennsylvania agriculture.\nThe free event will take place on Tuesday, April 7, from 8:30-10:30 a.m., at the Marion Volunteer Fire Company, 5465 Molly Pitcher Highway South, Chambersburg.\n“Agriculture plays a vital role in our local economy and way of life,” the three lawmakers said. “This breakfast is an opportunity for farmers and community members to connect directly with state leaders, hear the latest updates affecting the industry and share their perspectives.”\nPennsylvania Secretary of Agriculture Russell Redding is the keynote speaker and will offer updates on the state’s agriculture industry and discuss challenges and opportunities facing farmers across the Commonwealth.\n“Agriculture remains Pennsylvania’s top industry, and maintaining open communication with the people who feed and fuel our communities is essential,” the lawmakers said. “We encourage our valued farmers to join us for this informative morning.”\nThere is no cost to attend; however, RSVP is required. Residents may RSVP by calling 717-749-7384, or going online to\nRepReichard.com\n,\nRepKauffman.com\nor\nRepIrvin.com\n.\nRepresentative Chad Reichard\n90th Legislative District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Greg Gross\n717.260.6374\nggross@pahousegop.com\nRepReichard.com / Facebook.com/RepReichard\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "Three Republican state representatives from Franklin County are hosting a free agricultural breakfast event on April 7, 2026, in Chambersburg. The event will feature Pennsylvania Secretary of Agriculture Russell Redding as a keynote speaker and is open to farmers, agricultural workers, and residents. Attendance is free but requires an RSVP.",
      "action_type": "event",
      "topics": [
        "economy",
        "other"
      ],
      "spin_flag": false
    }
  },
