    "title": "Kauffman Announces State Funding for Sensory Learning Pathway at Memorial Park",
    "url": "https://www.repkauffman.com/News/35500/Press-Releases/Kauffman-Announces-State-Funding-for-Sensory-Learning-Pathway-at-Memorial-Park",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Kauffman Announces State Funding for Sensory Learning Pathway at Memorial Park\nJanuary 28, 2025\nHARRISBURG – Memorial Park in Chambersburg will get an exciting upgrade with the addition of a new sensory learning pathway, according to Rep. Rob Kauffman (R-Franklin), who supported funding for the project under the Greenways, Trails and Recreation Program.\n“State funding in the amount of $49,000 will enable this important project to be completed,” said Kauffman. “Our public parks and recreational areas need to be accessible to all and this new pathway will ensure those will disabilities have access to fun, engaging activities at the park.”\nThe funding will be used to purchase and install sensory learning panels and\r\nmusic chimes, and repaving and widening of a pathway at Memorial Park. The\r\nproposed project will aid the borough of Chambersburg by creating a park that is inclusive of\r\nindividuals with disabilities, through ensuring adequate play opportunities via playground\r\nequipment and wheelchair accessibility.\nFunding was awarded by the Commonwealth Financing Authority under the Greenways, Trails and Recreation Program.\nRepresentative Rob Kauffman\n89th District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "Memorial Park in Chambersburg, PA will receive $49,000 in state funding to install sensory learning panels, music chimes, and an accessible pathway. The money comes from the Commonwealth Financing Authority's Greenways, Trails and Recreation Program. Rep. Kauffman announced the grant and indicated he supported the funding for the project.",
      "action_type": "budget",
